    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45583" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφαιρέω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>take hold on, overspread</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ χλόος εἷλε παρειάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.1216
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Med.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐωχ-αιρέομαι</span></b> , aor.
			2 -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ειλόμην</span>, <i>choose as
				successor</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				49.43
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be chosen</i> or <i>appointed to succeed</i>
			another, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					4.38
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				9(1).694.93
			</span></i> (Corc.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅσσουν ἐφάνγρενθείν κινες</span>
			Thess. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅσων ἐφαιροῦνταί </span>( 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατηγοροῦσί</span>
			)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> τινες</span> whomsoever any persons
				<i>accuse</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				9(2).517.41
			</span></i> (Larissa, <span class="entity">iii B. C.</span>).</div>
